  "description": "Fuselage: Deep ocean blue all over. Cheatlines: None; from over the wing aft, a lighter sea-blue band of water with whitecaps runs along the middle of the fuselage to the tail, and a pod of orcas swims in it, the largest by the aft door. Tail: A printed photograph: Pacific Northwest forest at the top, a waterfall, and an orca breaching from blue water at the root. Engines: Ocean blue. Winglets: Alaska's standard (white with midnight, Atlas-blue and lime bands). Titles: The 2016 'Alaska' wordmark in white, large, forward of the wing. Artwork: Orcas (the Southern Resident pods) on the water band; the tail is inkjet-printed, the first image Boeing applied that way. Colors hex: not published; matched by eye.",
